Since I posted the list of existing law lists, several people have
contacted
me about how to subscribe to them.  Below is the list with
instructions for
subscribing included.  Good luck!  Lyo.  P.S.  Replace "Your Name",
"firstname lastname", etc. with your real name.  So for instance, if
Toshiro Mifune wanted to subscribe to INT-LAW, he'd send the following
message to the LISTSERV@UMINN1.BITNET:  subscribe int-law Toshiro
Mifune.
----------------------------------------
 
AI-L@austin.onu.edu (artificial intelligence and the law)
     (send the following message to the listserv@austin.onu.edu:
subscribe ai-l Your Name)
 
all-of-elsa@jus.uio.no (European Law Students Association list)
     (send your e-mail address and subscription request to the list
moderator, Arild Kvanvik Joergensen, akj@jus.nio.no)
 
BIZLAW-L@umab.umd.edu (AALS Section on Business Associations list for
law
faculty & practitioners)
     (send the following message to the listserv@umab.umd.edu (or
listserv@umab.bitnet):  sub bizlaw-l Firstname Lastname)
 
CALI-L@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu (US-based computer-assisted legal
instruction list)
     (send to the listserv@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu, the message:
subscribe cali-l Yourfirstname Yourlastname)
 
CALL-L@UNBVM1.BITNET (Canadian academic law libraries list)
     (send the following message to the listserv@unbvm1.bitnet:
subscribe call-l Your Name)
 
CJUST-L@iubvm.ucs.indiana.edu (criminal justice)
     (send the following message to the
listserv@iubvm.ucs.indiana.edu:  subscribe cjust-l Your Name)
 
CNI-COPYRIGHT@cni.org (copyright & intellectual property forum)
     (send the following message to the listserv@cni.org:  subscribe
cni-copyright Yourfirstname Yourlastname)
 
COMLAW-L@UALTAVM.BITNET (computers & legal education)
     (send the following message to the listserv@ualtavm.bitnet:
subscribe comlaw-l Your Name)
 
CTI-LAW@mailbase.ac.uk (UK-based list on use of information technology
in law teaching)
     (send the following message to the mailbase@mailbase.ac.uk:  join
cti-law firstname lastname)
 
CYBERIA-L@listserv.cc.wm.edu (the law and policy of computer networks;
formerly CYBERLAW/CYBERLAW-L)
     (send the following message to the listserv@listserv.cc.wm.edu
(or listserver@eagle.birds.wm.edu):
subscribe cyberia-l Your Name)
 
data-protection@mailbase.ac.uk (UK data protection law)
     (send the following message to the mailbase@mailbase.ac.uk:  join
data-protection Yourfirstname Yourlastname)
 
EDLAW@ukcc.uky.edu (law and education)
     (send the following message to the listserv@ukcc.uky.edu:
subscribe edlaw Your Name)
 
ENVLAWPROFS@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu (international discussion list for
professors of environmental law)
     (send the following message to the mailserv@oregon.uoregon.edu:
subscribe envlawprofs Your Name Here)
 
EURO-LEX@DEARN.BITNET (All EUROpean Legal Information
EXchange--discusses EC
& European country legal information sources mainly)
     (send the following message to the listserv@dearn.bitnet:
subscribe euro-lex Your Name)
 
FEDTAX-L@SHSU.BITNET (federal taxation)
     (send the following message to the listserv@shsu.bitnet:
subscribe fedtax-l Your Name)
 
FEMJUR@suvm.syr.edu (discussions & information about feminist legal
issues)
     (send the following message to the listserv@suvm.syr.edu (or
listserv@suvm.bitnet):  subscribe femjur Your Name)
 
H-LAW@uicvm.uic.edu (legal history & U.S. constitutional history)
     (send the following message to the listserv@uicvm.uic.edu (or
listserv@uicvm.bitnet):  subscribe H-Law Firstname Surname,
Yourschool)
 
HISLAW-L@ulkyvm.louisville.edu (canon, feudal, & common law)
     (send the following message to the listserv@ulkyvm.louisville.edu
(or listserv@ulkyvm.bitnet):  subscribe hislaw-l Your Name)
 
INFO-LAW@brl.mil (computers in law)
     (send the following message to info-law-request@brl.mil:
subscribe info-law Your Name)
 
INT-LAW@vm1.spcs.umn.edu (foreign & international law librarians
list--includes discussion of international legal print, electronic, &
"people" resources)
     (send the following message to the listserv@vm1.spcs.umn.edu (or
listserv@uminn1.bitnet):  subscribe int-law Your Name)
 
JURIST-L@nic.surfnet.nl (Dutch lawyers list--discussion in Dutch)
     (send the following message to the listserv@nic.surfnet.nl:
subscribe jurist-l Yourfirstname Yourlastname)
 
LAW-LIB@ucdavis.edu (US-based law librarians list)
     (send the following message to law-lib-request@ucdavis.edu (or
law-req@ucdavis.edu):  subscribe law-lib Your Name)
 
LAWPROF@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu (law professors & lecturers list)
     (send the following message to the
listserv@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu:  subscribe lawprof Your name,
Position, Institution)
 
LAWSCH-L@AUVM.BITNET (law students list)
     (send the following message to the listserv@auvm.bitnet (or
listserv@auvm.american.edu):  subscribe lawsch-l Your Name)
 
LAWSRC-L@fatty.law.cornell.edu (Internet law sources list)
     (send the following message to the
listserv@fatty.law.cornell.edu:  subscribe lawsrc-l Your full name)
 
LEGWRI-L@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu (list for legal writing instructors)
     (send the following message to the
listserv@chicagokent.kentlaw.edu:  subscribe legwri-l Your Name)
 
LIS-LAW@mailbase.ac.uk (UK-based legal information & law libraries
list)
     (send the following message to the mailbase@mailbase.ac.uk:  join
lis-law firstname lastname)
 
PSYLAW-L@UTEPA.BITNET (psychology & law list, international
discussion)
     (send the following message to the listserv@utepa.bitnet:
subscribe psylaw-l Your Name)
 
TEKNOIDS@fatty.law.cornell.edu (US-based list for law school computing
professionals)
     (send the following message to the
listserv@fatty.law.cornell.edu:  subscribe teknoids Your Full Name)
 
TLTP-LAW@mailbase.ac.uk (UK-based list on creating & using legal
computer
based learning materials)
     (send the following message to the mailbase@mailbase.ac.uk:  join
tltp-law firstname lastname)
 
